q q .843137 .878431 .917647 RG 62.3622 39.68504 m 532.9134 39.68504 l S .321569 .392157 .478431 rg BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.3622 24.09449 Tm T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 528.4654 24.09449 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 0 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT /F2 24 Tf 1 0 0 1 8.536 730 Tm (OS Analytics and Bottleneck Classifier)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 0 cm .321569 .392157 .478431 rg BT /F1 11.5 Tf 14.5 TL 1 0 0 1 42.671 706 Tm (A Modular Telemetry-Driven Framework for Operating System Bottleneck)Tj 1 0 0 1 81.644 691.5 Tm (Classification and LLM-Assisted Root-Cause Remediation)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 656.0236 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 13 TL/F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 68.55439 3.6 Tm <48696d616e73687520285341502049443a20353930303234383131292020207f20202053616b7368616d204d6568746120285341502049443a2035393030323536323829>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 640.0236 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 13 TL/F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 64.37609 3.6 Tm <4c617669736820477570746120285341502049443a20353930303236393331292020207f2020205069797573682053696e64687520285341502049443a2035393030323830383029>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 626.0236 cm .321569 .392157 .478431 rg BT 11 TL/F3 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 33.53334 2.5 Tm (B.Tech. Computer Science and Engineering | University of Petroleum and Energy Studies \(UPES\), India)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 612.9236 cm .101961 .65098 .717647 RG 1 J 1.1 w 0 0 m 458.5512 0 l S Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 591.9236 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 13 TL/F2 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm (Abstract)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 440.7236 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 2.146144 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 136.1 Tm (Operating-system performance degradation often emerges from interactions among CPU scheduling, memory pressure,)Tj T* 2.330959 Tw (storage I/O and other resource domains. Conventional threshold-based monitoring can produce noisy alerts or fail to)Tj T* 1.469806 Tw (distinguish the active bottleneck when several counters change together. This paper presents a modular telemetry-driven)Tj T* 2.281656 Tw (framework that samples operating-system counters, classifies four operational states, and connects the prediction to a)Tj T* 2.237144 Tw (structured root-cause analysis \(RCA\) assistant. The packaged implementation includes a workload-generation pipeline,)Tj T* -.061735 Tw (run-grouped preprocessing, a model benchmark suite, a Streamlit dashboard supporting live telemetry and CSV playback, and)Tj T* .865252 Tw (a Gemini-oriented diagnosis agent with an offline heuristic fallback. The included raw dataset contains 2,400 observations)Tj T* .347906 Tw (across 32 runs, balanced across Normal, CPU_Bound, Memory_Pressure and IO_Contention. The saved split contains 1,950)Tj T* 2.236699 Tw (training rows from 26 runs and 450 test rows from six disjoint runs. In the packaged benchmark artifact, XGBoost,)Tj T* .271199 Tw (LightGBM and Random Forest each report 100% held-out test accuracy and a Macro F1 of 1.0000; XGBoost has a recorded)Tj T* 1.113355 Tw (mean inference latency of 0.0071 ms. These results are promising within the controlled dataset, but they do not establish)Tj T* 0 Tw (production generalization. Further validation on independent hardware and real multi-tenant workloads is required.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 414.7236 cm .321569 .392157 .478431 rg BT 11 TL/F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 13.5 Tm (Index Terms:)Tj/F1 8.5 Tf ( Operating systems, performance telemetry, bottleneck classification, machine learning, XGBoost, grouped)Tj T* (validation, root-cause analysis, AIOps, large language models.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 391.7236 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 15 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (I. INTRODUCTION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 325.2236 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT .692406 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 51.4 Tm (Modern computing nodes execute diverse workloads that compete for processor time, physical memory, storage bandwidth)Tj T* .848872 Tw (and network capacity. The resulting performance symptoms are not always isolated. For example, sustained storage writes)Tj T* .318628 Tw (may trigger dirty-page writeback, increase kernel activity and leave processes waiting for I/O. A monitor that considers only)Tj T* .044178 Tw (one counter can misinterpret this coupled behavior. Tools such as top, vmstat, sar and iostat expose valuable telemetry, yet an)Tj T* 0 Tw (operator must still interpret signals across subsystems and decide what to investigate next.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 270.8236 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 1.700758 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm (The project addresses this gap with a two-tier design. A local machine-learning classifier maps numeric telemetry to a)Tj T* .749005 Tw (bottleneck class with low inference cost. A separate diagnosis component uses the predicted class and telemetry context to)Tj T* 2.419144 Tw (produce a structured explanation, investigation commands and remediation suggestions. Separating classification from)Tj T* 0 Tw (language-model assistance keeps the fast prediction path distinct from the slower, network-dependent explanation path.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 253.8236 cm .137255 .407843 .768627 rg BT 12 TL/F2 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (A. Problem Statement)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 211.5236 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT .257605 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 27.2 Tm (The objective is to build a reproducible and non-intrusive pipeline that samples OS performance counters at approximately 1)Tj T* .223468 Tw (Hz, classifies non-linear resource bottleneck regimes without row-level temporal leakage, and provides actionable root-cause)Tj T* 0 Tw (guidance. The four target classes are Normal, CPU_Bound, Memory_Pressure and IO_Contention.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 194.5236 cm .137255 .407843 .768627 rg BT 12 TL/F2 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (B. Contributions)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 152.2236 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT .276785 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 27.2 Tm (The implementation combines \(1\) configurable workload generation and telemetry capture, \(2\) a run-aware holdout split and)Tj T* .287581 Tw (grouped cross-validation for model evaluation, \(3\) comparison of a static heuristic with classical ML and neural models, and)Tj T* 0 Tw (\(4\) an interactive dashboard connected to an LLM-assisted RCA component with a deterministic local fallback.)Tj T* ET Q Q

