q q .843137 .878431 .917647 RG .5 w 62.3622 799.3701 m 532.9134 799.3701 l S .321569 .392157 .478431 rg BT 9 TL/F1 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.3622 809.2913 Tm (OS ANALYTICS & BOTTLENECK CLASSIFIER)Tj T* ET 62.3622 39.68504 m 532.9134 39.68504 l S BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.3622 24.09449 Tm T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 528.4654 24.09449 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 761.5276 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 15 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (VI. DISCUSSION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 707.1276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 2.540634 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm (The results support the project's design choice to keep numeric classification local and use the language model for)Tj T* .173527 Tw (explanation. The classical tree ensembles are competitive on the controlled tabular dataset, while the 1D CNN does not show)Tj T* 1.002638 Tw (a benefit in the reported test metrics. The static heuristic illustrates how fixed rules can underperform when the workload)Tj T* 0 Tw (signatures are more complex than the small set of manually selected thresholds.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 640.6276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT .817605 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 51.4 Tm (There are important validity limits. First, the sample population is a controlled synthetic dataset rather than a collection of)Tj T* .860468 Tw (independent production incidents. Second, six held-out runs provide limited evidence about variation across environments.)Tj T* .142105 Tw (Third, inference latency depends on hardware, software versions, batch shape and measurement method. Fourth, LLM output)Tj T* 1.217606 Tw (quality, API availability and remediation safety require separate evaluation from classifier accuracy. Finally, the reported)Tj T* 0 Tw (near-perfect test results should be replicated with newly generated runs and, ideally, real telemetry from distinct hosts.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 617.6276 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 15 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (VII. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE WORK)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 551.1276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 1.855168 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 51.4 Tm (This paper described a modular framework for classifying operating-system bottlenecks from telemetry and connecting)Tj T* 2.190816 Tw (predictions to structured root-cause guidance. The supplied implementation includes workload generation, run-grouped)Tj T* 1.107756 Tw (preprocessing, an eight-model benchmark suite, saved model artifacts, a Streamlit dashboard and a Gemini-oriented RCA)Tj T* .559786 Tw (component with an offline fallback. The packaged benchmark reports strong results for tree-based models on the controlled)Tj T* 0 Tw (held-out split, while the static-rule baseline performs substantially worse.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 496.7276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT .412072 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm (Future work should validate the classifier on real multi-tenant workloads and different hardware, report confidence intervals)Tj T* 1.739668 Tw (across repeated run-grouped splits, measure end-to-end dashboard and RCA latency, evaluate diagnosis correctness and)Tj T* 1.205318 Tw (command safety, explore eBPF-based telemetry, and extend the class set to additional conditions such as network socket)Tj T* 0 Tw (starvation and thread deadlock states.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 473.7276 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 15 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (ACKNOWLEDGMENT)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 443.5276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 1.225417 Tw 12.1 TL/F4 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 15.1 Tm (This paper was prepared from the supplied project dossier and the packaged OS Bottleneck Classifier code, datasets and)Tj T* 0 Tw (benchmark artifact. Mentor details were not supplied and are therefore not listed.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 420.5276 cm .062745 .129412 .227451 rg BT 15 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (REFERENCES)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 405.2276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.2 Tm ([1] B. Gregg, )Tj/F6 8.1 Tf (Systems Performance: Enterprise and the Cloud)Tj/F4 8.1 Tf (, 2nd ed. Addison-Wesley, 2020.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 380.6276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm <5b325d20542e204368656e20616e6420432e20477565737472696e2c20935847426f6f73743a2041205363616c61626c65205472656520426f6f7374696e672053797374656d2c9420696e20>Tj/F6 8.1 Tf (Proc. 22nd ACM SIGKDD Int. Conf. on Knowledge)Tj T* 16 0 Td (Discovery and Data Mining)Tj/F4 8.1 Tf (, 2016.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 356.0276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm <5b335d20472e204b6520657420616c2e2c20934c6967687447424d3a204120486967686c7920456666696369656e74204772616469656e7420426f6f7374696e67204465636973696f6e20547265652c9420696e20>Tj/F6 8.1 Tf (Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems)Tj/F4 8.1 Tf (,)Tj T* 16 0 Td (2017.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 341.7276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.2 Tm <5b345d204c2e20427265696d616e2c209352616e646f6d20466f72657374732c9420>Tj/F6 8.1 Tf (Machine Learning)Tj/F4 8.1 Tf <2c20766f6c2e2034352c206e6f2e20312c2070702e20359633322c20323030312e>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 327.4276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.2 Tm <5b355d20462e205065647265676f736120657420616c2e2c20935363696b69742d6c6561726e3a204d616368696e65204c6561726e696e6720696e20507974686f6e2c9420>Tj/F6 8.1 Tf (Journal of Machine Learning Research)Tj/F4 8.1 Tf <2c20766f6c2e2031322c2070702e203238323596323833302c20323031312e>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 302.8276 cm .133333 .168627 .211765 rg BT 10.3 TL/F4 8.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm <5b365d20476f6f676c6520446565704d696e642c209347656d696e693a20412046616d696c79206f6620486967686c792043617061626c65204d756c74696d6f64616c204d6f64656c732c9420323032342e2050726f6a65637420646f7373696572207265666572656e63653b206269626c696f677261706869632064657461696c73>Tj T* 16 0 Td (should be verified before formal submission.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 68.3622 259.3276 cm .929412 .952941